// Diagnostics: one `Diag` type for every stage (error, warning, help, fix), rustc-shaped rendering with
// source context, opt-in color (`J3C_COLOR=1`), and the near-name / did-you-mean helper.
//
// Port of: j3c/src/diag.rs, parse/error.rs, check/error.rs
// J3: Rust had three error types (parse, check, diag); one list of `Diag` replaces them (plan 11 B3):
// `struct Diag { code: u32, severity: Severity, span: Span, msg: string, notes: []Note, fix: Option<Fix> }`,
// appended to the `Session`'s list, never thrown. Every error site gets a stable code (`E0042`) when it is
// ported; a code is never reused or renumbered. Codes, titles and long explanations live in `text/errors.txt` (B10,
// embedded; `j3c explain` reads the same file); stages raise them by code, this module defines the type. Until parity (plan 11 D1) the renderer prints exactly what Rust printed
// (no code shown) and the driver stops after the first error. Tests and the LSP key off codes, not text.
module j3c.base.diag;
